IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 5 to 7A: "Act", the general provisions about enactments, "prescribed", and references to provisions.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.

§ `s 5: the word "Act"`

-- src:65 | (1) The word
-- src:67 | Act used in relation to a legislative enactment, shall include all Acts and ordinances which have been duly made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by any council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania, and to which assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign.
@ref s 5(1) (src:65-67)
GIVEN `made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by a council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1): an Act or ordinance is within the word Act used in relation to a legislative enactment` `made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by a council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania` `assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign` MEANS
    IF `made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by a council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania` AND `assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:69 | (2) In any Act, including this Act, a reference to an Act (including a reference to the Act in which the reference occurs) or to an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act includes a reference to any regulation made under that Act, Imperial Act, or Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 5(2) (src:69)
GIVEN `the thing referred to` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the regulation is made under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `the thing referred to` `the regulation is made under that Act` MEANS
    IF (`the thing referred to` EQUALS `an Act` OR `the thing referred to` EQUALS `an Imperial Act` OR `the thing referred to` EQUALS `a Commonwealth Act`) AND `the regulation is made under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 5(1): an Act or ordinance is within the word Act used in relation to a legislative enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1): an Act or ordinance is within the word Act used in relation to a legislative enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1): an Act or ordinance is within the word Act used in relation to a legislative enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `an Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `an Imperial Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `a Commonwealth Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `an Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a regulation made under it` `a proclamation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 6: general provisions as to legislative enactments`

-- src:73 | (1) Every section of an Act shall have effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
@ref s 6(1) (src:73)
GIVEN `the provision is a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1): a section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` `the provision is a section of an Act` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a section of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The parts of the printed text of an Act that ss 6(2) to (4) sort into "part of the Act" and "not part of the Act".
DECLARE `Element of the printed text of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act`
    `a schedule or appendix to the Act`
    `a heading of a schedule or appendix, or of a part, division or subdivision of one`
    `a heading to a provision of the Act`
    `a marginal note in the Act`
    `a footnote in the Act`
    `an endnote in the Act`
    `a footnote appended to a prescribed form`
    `a section of the Act`

-- src:75 | (2) The headings of the parts, divisions, and subdivisions, into which any Act is divided shall be deemed to be part of the Act.
@ref s 6(2) (src:75)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of the printed text of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a heading of a part, division or subdivision` element MEANS
    IF element EQUALS `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:77 | (3) Every schedule and appendix to an Act (including any heading of such a schedule or appendix or of any part, division or subdivision into which such a schedule or appendix is divided) shall be deemed to be part thereof.
@ref s 6(3) (src:77)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of the printed text of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(3): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a schedule, appendix or heading within one` element MEANS
    IF element EQUALS `a schedule or appendix to the Act` OR element EQUALS `a heading of a schedule or appendix, or of a part, division or subdivision of one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:79 | (4) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3) –
-- src:81 | (a) a heading to a provision of an Act; or
-- src:83 | (b) a marginal note, footnote or endnote in an Act (other than a footnote appended to a prescribed form) –
-- src:85 | shall not be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref s 6(4) (src:79-85)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of the printed text of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` element MEANS
    BRANCH IF element EQUALS `a heading to a provision of the Act` OR element EQUALS `a marginal note in the Act` OR element EQUALS `a footnote in the Act` OR element EQUALS `an endnote in the Act`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           IF element EQUALS `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act` OR element EQUALS `a schedule or appendix to the Act` OR element EQUALS `a heading of a schedule or appendix, or of a part, division or subdivision of one`
           THEN JUST FALSE   -- fork: "Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3)" met
           IF element EQUALS `a footnote appended to a prescribed form` THEN JUST FALSE   -- fork: "(other than a footnote appended to a prescribed form)"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- what the list does not name

-- src:75 | (2) The headings of the parts, divisions, and subdivisions, into which any Act is divided shall be deemed to be part of the Act.
-- src:77 | (3) Every schedule and appendix to an Act (including any heading of such a schedule or appendix or of any part, division or subdivision into which such a schedule or appendix is divided) shall be deemed to be part thereof.
-- src:79 | (4) Except as provided in subsections (2) and (3) –
-- src:81 | (a) a heading to a provision of an Act; or
-- src:83 | (b) a marginal note, footnote or endnote in an Act (other than a footnote appended to a prescribed form) –
-- src:85 | shall not be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref s 6(2), (3) and (4) (src:75-85)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of the printed text of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` element MEANS
    BRANCH IF `s 6(2): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a heading of a part, division or subdivision` element EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `s 6(3): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a schedule, appendix or heading within one` element EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` element EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 6(1): a section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1): a section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a heading of a part, division or subdivision` `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a heading of a part, division or subdivision` `a heading to a provision of the Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a schedule, appendix or heading within one` `a schedule or appendix to the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(3): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a schedule, appendix or heading within one` `a heading of a schedule or appendix, or of a part, division or subdivision of one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(3): the element is deemed to be part of the Act as a schedule, appendix or heading within one` `a marginal note in the Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a heading to a provision of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a marginal note in the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a footnote in the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `an endnote in the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a footnote appended to a prescribed form` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a schedule or appendix to the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(4): the element is not taken to be part of the Act` `a section of the Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` `the heading of a part, division or subdivision of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` `a schedule or appendix to the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` `a heading to a provision of the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` `a footnote appended to a prescribed form` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) to (4): the element is part of the Act` `a section of the Act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:87 | (5) An Act may be altered, amended, or repealed in the same session of Parliament as that in which it was passed.
@ref s 6(5) (src:87)
GIVEN `in the same session of Parliament as that in which it was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(5): an Act may be altered, amended or repealed` `in the same session of Parliament as that in which it was passed` MEANS
    IF `in the same session of Parliament as that in which it was passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:89 | (6) No Act shall be binding on the Crown or derogate from any prerogative right of the Crown unless express words are included therein for that purpose.
@ref s 6(6) (src:89)
GIVEN `express words are included in the Act for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(6): an Act is not binding on the Crown and does not derogate from a prerogative right of the Crown` `express words are included in the Act for that purpose` MEANS
    IF `express words are included in the Act for that purpose` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- fork: "unless" met

-- src:91 | (7) Every Act passed after 5th August 1853 shall be a public Act and shall be judicially noticed as such unless the contrary is expressly provided by that Act.
@ref s 6(7) (src:91)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed` IS A DATE
      `the contrary is expressly provided by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(7): an Act is a public Act judicially noticed as such` `the day the Act was passed` `the contrary is expressly provided by the Act` MEANS
    IF `s 6(7): an Act was passed after 5th August 1853` `the day the Act was passed`
    THEN JUST (NOT (`the contrary is expressly provided by the Act`))
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 6(5): an Act may be altered, amended or repealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(5): an Act may be altered, amended or repealed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(6): an Act is not binding on the Crown and does not derogate from a prerogative right of the Crown` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(6): an Act is not binding on the Crown and does not derogate from a prerogative right of the Crown` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(7): an Act is a public Act judicially noticed as such` (Date 6 8 1853) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(7): an Act is a public Act judicially noticed as such` (Date 6 8 1853) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(7): an Act is a public Act judicially noticed as such` (Date 5 8 1853) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(7): an Act is a public Act judicially noticed as such` (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 7: "prescribed"`

-- src:97 | (a) means prescribed by, or by regulations made under, the Act in which the word appears; and
@ref s 7(a) (src:97)
GIVEN `prescribed by the Act in which the word appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulations made under the Act in which the word appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(a): a thing is prescribed for the Act in which the word prescribed appears` `prescribed by the Act in which the word appears` `prescribed by regulations made under the Act in which the word appears` MEANS
    JUST (`prescribed by the Act in which the word appears` OR `prescribed by regulations made under the Act in which the word appears`)

-- src:99 | (b) where reference is made to anything prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears, includes anything prescribed by any regulation made under that other Act.
@ref s 7(b) (src:99)
GIVEN `prescribed by regulations made under the other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(b): a thing prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears includes a thing prescribed by regulation made under that other Act` `prescribed by regulations made under the other Act` MEANS
    IF `prescribed by regulations made under the other Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 7(a): a thing is prescribed for the Act in which the word prescribed appears` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(a): a thing is prescribed for the Act in which the word prescribed appears` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(a): a thing is prescribed for the Act in which the word prescribed appears` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(b): a thing prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears includes a thing prescribed by regulation made under that other Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(b): a thing prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears includes a thing prescribed by regulation made under that other Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7A: references to provisions of Acts`

-- src:103 | (1) Where in an Act reference is made to a Part, division, section, Schedule, or form without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule, or form of some other Act is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule, or form of the Act in which the reference is made.
@ref s 7A(1) (src:103)
GIVEN `the context indicates a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form of some other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(1): a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form is a reference to one of the Act in which the reference is made` `the context indicates a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form of some other Act` MEANS
    JUST (NOT (`the context indicates a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form of some other Act`))

-- src:105 | (2) Where in a section of an Act reference is made to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of some other section or provision is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of the section in which the reference is made.
@ref s 7A(2) (src:105)
GIVEN `the context indicates a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other section or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(2): a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division is a reference to one of the section in which the reference is made` `the context indicates a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other section or provision` MEANS
    JUST (NOT (`the context indicates a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other section or provision`))

-- src:107 | (2A) For the purposes of the application of subsections (1) and (2) to regulations, "section" and "subsection" shall be read as "regulation" and "subregulation", respectively.
@ref s 7A(2A) (src:107)
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 7A(2A): the word read in place of section or subsection when ss 7A(1) and (2) are applied to regulations` word MEANS
    BRANCH IF word EQUALS "section" THEN JUST "regulation"
           IF word EQUALS "subsection" THEN JUST "subregulation"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:109 | (3) Where in a Schedule or part of a Schedule to an Act reference is made to a clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of some other provision is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to the clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of the Schedule or the part of the Schedule in which the reference is made.
@ref s 7A(3) (src:109)
GIVEN `the context indicates a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7A(3): a reference in a Schedule to a clause or other division is a reference to one of the Schedule or part of the Schedule in which the reference is made` `the context indicates a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other provision` MEANS
    JUST (NOT (`the context indicates a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of some other provision`))

#ASSERT `s 7A(1): a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form is a reference to one of the Act in which the reference is made` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1): a reference to a Part, division, section, Schedule or form is a reference to one of the Act in which the reference is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2): a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division is a reference to one of the section in which the reference is made` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2): a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division is a reference to one of the section in which the reference is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2A): the word read in place of section or subsection when ss 7A(1) and (2) are applied to regulations` "section" EQUALS JUST "regulation"
#ASSERT `s 7A(2A): the word read in place of section or subsection when ss 7A(1) and (2) are applied to regulations` "subsection" EQUALS JUST "subregulation"
#ASSERT `s 7A(2A): the word read in place of section or subsection when ss 7A(1) and (2) are applied to regulations` "Schedule" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(3): a reference in a Schedule to a clause or other division is a reference to one of the Schedule or part of the Schedule in which the reference is made` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3): a reference in a Schedule to a clause or other division is a reference to one of the Schedule or part of the Schedule in which the reference is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
